ond, that the cost of innovation stagnation is greater than the cost of institutional disruption. If the first is wrong, then AI intelligence is a mirage, and the debate is moot. If the second is wrong, and the social cost of rapid disruption outweighs the benefits of AI advancement, then my accelerationist model fails to justify its own risks. We must stop viewing innovation as a threat to be managed and start viewing it as the primary moral imperative of our species. By choosing to throttle the development of intelligence, we are choosing a future of relative poverty and diminished capacity. ⚡",
